---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";

const lastUpdated = "May 21, 2026";
const contactEmail = "info@blockprint.la";
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy Policy — Blockprint"
  description="How Blockprint collects, uses, and protects information you share with us."
>
  <article class="privacy mx-auto max-w-2xl px-5 md:px-8 py-16 md:py-24">
    <!-- Wordmark links back to home -->
    <a
      href="/"
      class="block mb-12 md:mb-16"
      aria-label="Back to Blockprint home"
    >
      <img
        src="/brand/wordmark.png"
        alt="Blockprint"
        width="1010"
        height="152"
        class="w-full max-w-[360px] mx-auto"
      />
    </a>

    <header class="mb-10 md:mb-14 text-center">
      <h1 class="text-2xl md:text-3xl uppercase tracking-[0.3em] font-bold">
        Privacy Policy
      </h1>
      <p class="mt-3 text-xs md:text-sm uppercase tracking-[0.3em] opacity-60">
        Last updated · {lastUpdated}
      </p>
    </header>

    <div class="prose-content text-base leading-relaxed space-y-5">
      <p>
        Blockprint is a music festival produced by Clavette Entertainment,
        LLC ("Blockprint," "we," "us"). This Privacy Policy explains what
        information we collect when you interact with this website, how we
        use it, who we share it with, and the choices you have. By using
        the site or submitting your phone number through our signup form,
        you agree to the practices described below.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-lg md:text-xl uppercase tracking-[0.2em] font-bold pt-6">
        Information we collect
      </h2>
      <p>
        <strong>Information you give us.</strong> When you sign up for
        text-message alerts, we collect the mobile phone number you
        submit and a record of your consent to receive marketing
        messages from us.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Information collected automatically.</strong> When you
        visit the site, our hosting and analytics providers
        automatically receive standard request data — IP address,
        browser type, device type, referring page, the pages you view,
        and the date and time of your visit. We use this data in
        aggregate to understand how the site is performing.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-lg md:text-xl uppercase tracking-[0.2em] font-bold pt-6">
        How we use information
      </h2>
      <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2">
        <li>
          To send you text-message updates about Blockprint — including
          ticket on-sales, lineup announcements, schedule changes, and
          related festival news.
        </li>
        <li>
          To operate, secure, and improve the website and our marketing.
        </li>
        <li>
          To comply with legal obligations and enforce our terms.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2 class="text-lg md:text-xl uppercase tracking-[0.2em] font-bold pt-6">
        Third-party services we rely on
      </h2>
      <p>
        We use a small number of vendors to run the site and our
        messaging program. Each is contractually bound to use your
        information only to provide their service to us.
      </p>
      <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2">
        <li>
          <strong>Hive (Hive.co)</strong> — our SMS marketing platform.
          When you submit the signup form, your phone number and consent
          record are stored by Hive on our behalf and used to deliver
          messages. See
          <a
            href="https://hive.co/privacy"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener"
            class="underline">Hive's Privacy Policy</a
          >.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Vercel</strong> — our website host. Vercel processes
          request data to serve the site. See
          <a
            href="https://vercel.com/legal/privacy-policy"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener"
            class="underline">Vercel's Privacy Policy</a
          >.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Google Analytics 4</strong> — our website analytics
          provider. Google receives standard request data (IP address,
          browser, pages viewed, referrer) and uses it to give us
          aggregate, anonymized traffic insights. See
          <a
            href="https://policies.google.com/privacy"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener"
            class="underline">Google's Privacy Policy</a
          >.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Meta (Facebook) Pixel</strong> — used to measure the
          effectiveness of our ads on Facebook and Instagram and to
          show relevant ads to people who have visited the site. Meta
          receives the pages you view, your browser and device, and a
          pseudonymous identifier. See
          <a
            href="https://www.facebook.com/privacy/policy"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener"
            class="underline">Meta's Privacy Policy</a
          >.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2 class="text-lg md:text-xl uppercase tracking-[0.2em] font-bold pt-6">
        Text messaging program
      </h2>
      <p>
        By submitting the signup form, you expressly consent to receive
        recurring marketing text messages from Blockprint at the mobile
        number you provided. Consent is not a condition of any purchase.
        Message frequency varies. Message and data rates may apply.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>To stop messages,</strong> reply <strong>STOP</strong> to
        any text. <strong>For help,</strong> reply <strong>HELP</strong>
        or contact us at the email below. Carriers are not liable for
        delayed or undelivered messages.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-lg md:text-xl uppercase tracking-[0.2em] font-bold pt-6">
        Sharing your information
      </h2>
      <p>
        We do not sell your personal information. We share it only with
        the vendors listed above, with our legal and professional
        advisors, in connection with a sale or restructuring of the
        business, or when we are required to do so by law.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-lg md:text-xl uppercase tracking-[0.2em] font-bold pt-6">
        Data retention
      </h2>
      <p>
        We keep your phone number and consent record for as long as you
        remain subscribed to our messages, and for a reasonable period
        afterwards to maintain proof of consent and honor opt-out
        requests. Aggregated usage analytics are retained on a rolling
        basis per our analytics provider's standard retention.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-lg md:text-xl uppercase tracking-[0.2em] font-bold pt-6">
        Your choices and rights
      </h2>
      <p>
        You can opt out of marketing texts at any time by replying STOP.
        You can also email us at <a
          href={`mailto:${contactEmail}`}
          class="underline">{contactEmail}</a
        > to request access to, correction of, or deletion of the
        personal information we hold about you.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>California residents</strong> have additional rights
        under the California Consumer Privacy Act, including the right
        to know what personal information we collect about you, the
        right to request deletion, the right to opt out of any sale or
        sharing of personal information (we do not sell), and the right
        not to be discriminated against for exercising these rights. To
        exercise any of these rights, contact us at the email above.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-lg md:text-xl uppercase tracking-[0.2em] font-bold pt-6">
        Cookies and tracking
      </h2>
      <p>
        The site sets a small number of cookies. Google Analytics 4
        sets cookies (such as <code>_ga</code> and <code>_ga_*</code>)
        to distinguish unique visitors and measure session activity.
        The Meta Pixel sets cookies (such as <code>_fbp</code>) to
        attribute ad performance and enable retargeting on Facebook
        and Instagram. Vercel may set cookies for hosting and
        performance purposes.
      </p>
      <p>
        You can block or limit these cookies through your browser
        settings. For analytics specifically, install the
        <a
          href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener"
          class="underline">Google Analytics opt-out browser add-on</a
        >. For Meta's advertising cookies, adjust your
        <a
          href="https://www.facebook.com/adpreferences"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener"
          class="underline">Facebook ad preferences</a
        >.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-lg md:text-xl uppercase tracking-[0.2em] font-bold pt-6">
        Children
      </h2>
      <p>
        Blockprint is a 21-and-over event and this site is intended for
        an adult audience. We do not knowingly collect personal
        information from minors. If you believe someone under 18 has
        submitted information to us, please contact us and we will delete
        it.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-lg md:text-xl uppercase tracking-[0.2em] font-bold pt-6">
        Changes to this policy
      </h2>
      <p>
        We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. When we do,
        we will revise the "Last updated" date at the top of this page.
        Material changes will be communicated by posting the updated
        policy here; if the change affects how we use information you've
        already given us, we'll notify SMS subscribers via text first.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-lg md:text-xl uppercase tracking-[0.2em] font-bold pt-6">
        Contact us
      </h2>
      <p>
        Questions about this policy or how we handle your information?
        Email us at <a
          href={`mailto:${contactEmail}`}
          class="underline">{contactEmail}</a
        >.
      </p>
      <p class="text-sm opacity-70 pt-4">
        Clavette Entertainment, LLC
      </p>
    </div>

    <footer class="mt-16 text-center">
      <a
        href="/"
        class="inline-block text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.4em] underline decoration-ink/40 underline-offset-4 hover:decoration-ink"
      >
        ← Back
      </a>
    </footer>
  </article>
</Layout>

<style>
  /* Anchor styling within the policy body — keep underlines but use the
     brand ink color and a comfortable underline offset for readability. */
  .prose-content a {
    text-decoration-thickness: 1px;
    text-underline-offset: 3px;
  }
</style>
